{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes a conservative exploration policy: random_walk is used for coverage in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used when obstacles are detected. Recovery direction is chosen based on which side is blocked, and full_rotate is reserved for deadlock (all sides blocked). The supervisor always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear, and never enables unsafe actions in obstacle states.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, deterministic recovery and exploration, prioritizing safety and steady progress, and avoiding oscillations or unsafe loops."
  ],
